  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="HH2FB9527C1D4BB25D79F1C0C76F5BC95D" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
		&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:8pt; font-size:8pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;Monongahela Power Company (MP) has authorization from the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) to issue short-term debt of up to $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;9&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;00 million through bank facilities and FirstEnergy&amp;#x2019;s regulated money pool,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;and has authorization from the West Virginia Service Commission (WVPSC) to participate in the regulated money pool.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;MP has the ability to borrow from its regulated affiliates and FirstEnergy Corp, (FE) to meet its short-term working capital requirements. FirstEnergy Service Company administers this money pool and tracks surplus funds of FirstEnergy and the respective regulated subsidiary, as well as proceeds available from bank borrowings. Companies receiving a loan under the money pool agreements must repay the principal amount of the loan, together with accrued interest, within 364 days of borrowing the funds. The rate of interest &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;is the same for each company receiving a loan from their respective pool and is based on the average cost of funds available through the pool. The average interest rate for borrowings for the first &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;six&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; months of 2026 was 4.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;9&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;% per annum.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:8pt; font-size:8pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;In &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;May&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;, 2026 M&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;P&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; issued $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; million of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;4.45&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;% &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;first mortgage bonds&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; due in 20&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;29&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
		&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;
	&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
